    "message": "Operation 'post-transfers' has semantic quality issues: missing_output_details, missing_side_effects. Summary is clear and actionable. Description has good context about supported destinations and permission requirements, but lacks clarity on the asynchronous nature of the operation and what the response contains. Added explicit mention of the 202 Accepted status code, clarified that this is asynchronous with webhook delivery, specified the request schema (TransferInfo), and emphasized that 202 means acceptance not completion. This helps AI agents understand they must handle asynchronous callbacks and not treat the response as confirmation of transfer completion.",
